      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In APA 7th edition, for a paper with 6 authors, you would typically list all authors in the in-text citation until the sixth author, then use \"et al.\" (short for et alii, meaning \"and others\") as a shorthand for the remaining authors. This would look like: (Smith, Johnson, Thompson, et al.). In Chicago style, the method can vary depending on the style (note, there are different editions of Chicago), but generally, if there are 6 authors, you would list all authors in the in-text citation and then use \"et al.\" after the sixth author(s).",
